{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["You shall not curse the deaf — Scripture speaks of a case where it applies. And its reason: the resh carries a dagesh, for it is a משקל (noun-pattern) with a doubled letter — like עִוֵּר, גִּבֵּן."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "The lemma חרש has no dagesh in the resh in the standard Textus; Rashbam apparently reads or discusses it as though it should or could carry one, comparing it to noun-patterns with doubled middle radicals."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:49:02.957235211Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}